  "id": "DrugBank_DB11757 - MONDO_18321",
  "verbalization": "Istradefylline is associated with Atypical Juvenile Parkinsonism through a chain of indications that link it to X-linked Parkinsonism-spasticity Syndrome, which in turn is indicated by Entacapone, Rasagiline, and Pimavanserin. This suggests that Istradefylline may exert a therapeutic effect on Atypical Juvenile Parkinsonism via a pathway involving these medications. The evidence highlights a potential mechanism where Istradefylline could influence the disease through its interaction with these indicated agents, possibly by modulating neurotransmitter systems or other biological processes. The recurring association with X-linked Parkinsonism-spasticity Syndrome implies a broader role in Parkinsonian pathology, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The integration of these indications supports a hypothesis that Istradefylline may have a role in the treatment of Atypical Juvenile Parkinsonism, though further research is needed to confirm the direct relationship.",
